  recipeId: motor
  concept: 'Authored objective: Repair three independent drive faults.

    Authored
    requirement: Diagnose and repair phase V, the encoder via and the regenerative
    brake sensor, with a fresh test after each.

    General teaching principle:
    Motor behavior depends on drive conditions, load, feedback and protective limits;
    test the observed state at each authored checkpoint.

    Only fresh, authoritative
    game evidence can establish that this objective is complete.'
  analogy: A controlled wheel under varying load shows why a command does not always
    equal actual speed.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: A drive command alone does not establish speed, torque or safe stopping.
  baseline: "Before working on \u2018Repair three independent drive faults\u2019,
    which component, reference or condition mentioned in the authored requirement
    should you inspect first? Explain your reasoning."
  prediction: "For \u2018Repair three independent drive faults\u2019, what result
    or observation would you expect if the required setup is correct? Distinguish
    a predicted result from a measured result."
  practice: "In Level 119, perform the objective \u2018Repair three independent drive
    faults\u2019 in the actual game laboratory. Compare fresh evidence against: Diagnose
    and repair phase V, the encoder via and the regenerative brake sensor, with a
    fresh test after each.\nThe mission evaluator decides completion; this tutorial
    does not grade your answer."
